SUMMARY:Mocktails & Meaning™: Public Health in Lancaster County
DESCRIPTION:Discover how public health impacts all of us at Mocktails & Meaning™ on Thursday\, October 15\, 2026\, at 6:30 PM in the Main Lobby. Retired surgeon and public health advocate Dr. Edward Chory\, who serves on the Board of the Partnership for Public Health\, will lead a conversation about the current state of public health in Lancaster County and the potential benefits of establishing a county health department. Together\, we’ll explore how public health initiatives influence the well-being of our communities\, what a local health department could mean for Lancaster County\, and why these conversations matter to all of us. We’ll be serving a mocktail (to be announced) 🍹\, with plenty of time for questions\, discussion\, and meaningful dialogue.
URL:https://apostlesucc.org/event/mocktails-meaning-public-health-in-lancaster-county/
LOCATION:Church of the Apostles UCC\, 1850 Marietta Ave\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://apostlesucc.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Mocktails-Meaning-Slide-10.15.26-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
